{
	title: 'Show a task',
	spec: 'tsk show <id> displays ID, title, full spec (not obsolete description), status, optional once, notes and foldInto, dependencies with ID/title/status, dependent IDs, incoming fold links as foldedBy, and task artifacts. Human output omits empty sections; structured --format json|ason includes empty lists; report unknown IDs clearly. tsk ls sorts by ID; compact human rows show status, ID, title, nonempty needs/note/file counts, approximately 80-column spec excerpt and byte size, plus planned/done totals (pad DONE only with planned rows). --status (space or =), --spec, --notes and --folded-by filter or expand output; structured summaries include ID, title, status, needs, noteCount, Unicode-code-point specLength and requested optional fields. tsk tree draws branch connectors from prerequisite roots to dependents; an ID limits to that task and downstream. Shared descendants expand once, later links name the additional parent; annotate foldInto targets separately. Structured graph output contains sorted nodes, prerequisite-to-dependent edges and separate foldInto edges. Errors go to stderr; data commands default to human output and accept --format json|ason.',
